Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how we will use them  
• `birth_death_growth_rates.country_code` – join key that links migration data with the area table  
• `birth_death_growth_rates.country_name` – readable country label to show in the result  
• `birth_death_growth_rates.year` – filter to the target year (2017)  
• `birth_death_growth_rates.net_migration` – the migration rate we need to rank by (per‑1,000 population)  

• `country_names_area.country_code` – join key coming from the area table  
• `country_names_area.country_area` – apply the “area > 500 km²” constraint  
• `country_names_area.country_name` – (optional) readable label from the area table  

Typical conditions  
• `b.year = 2017` – keep only 2017 records  
• `a.country_area > 500` – exclude micro‑states / small territories  
• `b.net_migration IS NOT NULL` – avoid nulls when ranking  
• `ORDER BY b.net_migration DESC` – sort from highest to lowest  
• `LIMIT 3` – top‑3 list required by the task  

Below are 10 BigQuery SQL examples (each capped at 20 rows) moving from simple inspection to the final answer.  
(Replace nothing—table and column names are already fully‑qualified; back‑ticks are used throughout.)

```sql
-- 1. Quick peek at migration data
SELECT country_code, country_name, year, net_migration
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Which years are available in the migration table?
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates`
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Net‑migration figures for 2017 (unordered preview)
SELECT country_code, country_name, net_migration
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates`
WHERE year = 2017
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Countries with land area larger than 500 km²
SELECT country_code, country_name, country_area
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area`
WHERE country_area > 500
ORDER BY country_area DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Join area + migration for 2017, show biggest migration values
SELECT b.country_code,
       b.country_name,
       b.net_migration,
       a.country_area
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates` AS b
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area`        AS a
  ON b.country_code = a.country_code
WHERE b.year = 2017
  AND a.country_area > 500
ORDER BY b.net_migration DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same as #5 but exclude nulls explicitly
SELECT b.country_code,
       b.country_name,
       b.net_migration,
       a.country_area
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates` b
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area` a
  ON b.country_code = a.country_code
WHERE b.year = 2017
  AND a.country_area > 500
  AND b.net_migration IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY b.net_migration DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add ranking (without the area filter yet, just 2017)
SELECT country_code,
       country_name,
       net_migration,
       RANK() OVER (ORDER BY net_migration DESC) AS migration_rank
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates`
WHERE year = 2017
ORDER BY migration_rank
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Rank after applying the “area > 500” condition
SELECT b.country_code,
       b.country_name,
       b.net_migration,
       a.country_area,
       RANK() OVER (ORDER BY b.net_migration DESC) AS migration_rank
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates` b
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area` a
  ON b.country_code = a.country_code
WHERE b.year = 2017
  AND a.country_area > 500
ORDER BY migration_rank
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Straightforward top‑3 answer query (single SELECT, no CTE)
SELECT b.country_code,
       b.country_name,
       b.net_migration
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates` b
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area` a
  ON b.country_code = a.country_code
WHERE b.year = 2017
  AND a.country_area > 500
ORDER BY b.net_migration DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

```sql
-- 10. Same logic as #9 but written with CTEs for clarity (final answer version)
WITH area_filter AS (
  SELECT country_code, country_area
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.country_names_area`
  WHERE country_area > 500
),
migration_2017 AS (
  SELECT country_code, country_name, net_migration
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.birth_death_growth_rates`
  WHERE year = 2017
)
SELECT m.country_name,
       m.net_migration
FROM migration_2017 m
JOIN area_filter a USING (country_code)
ORDER BY m.net_migration DESC
LIMIT 3;
```

